{"title":"The Future Was Then: an Exhibition of Fascist Italian Posters","link":"https://kottke.org/25/09/the-future-was-then-an-exhibition-of-fascist-italian-posters","date":1759255858000,"content":"\n        <p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/ph-italy-fascism-01.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/ph-italy-fascism-01.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/ph-italy-fascism-01.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"890\" alt=\"a pair of early 20th century Italian posters\" /></p>\n\n<p>Speaking of <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/09/mussolini-son-of-the-century\">Benito Mussolini and fascism</a>, the excellent <a href=\"https://posterhouse.org\">Poster House museum</a> in NYC has a new exhibition on for the next few months: <a href=\"https://posterhouse.org/exhibition/the-future-was-then-the-changing-face-of-fascist-italy/\">The Future Was Then: The Changing Face of Fascist Italy</a>. It features “some of the best posters produced during the worst period in modern Italian history”.</p>\n\n<blockquote><p>In a fascist movement inspired by art, how does the fascist government influence the artists living in its grasp? This exhibition explores how Benito Mussolini’s government created a broad-reaching culture that grew with and into the Futurist movement to claw into advertising, propaganda, and the very heart of the nation he commanded.</p></blockquote>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/ph-italy-fascism-02.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/ph-italy-fascism-02.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/ph-italy-fascism-02.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"1836\" alt=\"a poster for Fiat with a man wearing oil cans on each of his hands and feet\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/ph-italy-fascism-03.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/ph-italy-fascism-03.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/ph-italy-fascism-03.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"899\" alt=\"a pair of early 20th century Italian posters\" /></p>\n\n<p>That Lubrificanti Fiat poster is incredible. <a href=\"https://posterhouse.org/exhibition/the-future-was-then-the-changing-face-of-fascist-italy/\">The Future Was Then</a> is on view at Poster House  until Feb 22, 2026.</p>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/advertising\">advertising</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/art\">art</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Benito%20Mussolini\">Benito Mussolini</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Italy\">Italy</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/museums\">museums</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/NYC\">NYC</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/politics\">politics</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Poster%20House\">Poster House</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/09/the-future-was-then-an-exhibition-of-fascist-italian-posters\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"c25e44dd5c041271f8525690d897d665c010ace83d506db9d8e8ae2eaaa6fdb4","category":"Sites"}